Add a Vite alias (and matching TypeScript path) that maps '@' to the 'src' directory. For example, create or update `vite.config.ts`:
```ts
import { defineConfig } from 'vite';
import react from '@vitejs/plugin-react';
import path from 'path';

export default defineConfig({
  plugins: [react()],
  resolve: {
    alias: {
      '@': path.resolve(__dirname, 'src'),
    },
  },
});
```
And update `tsconfig.json` (or `tsconfig.app.json`) to include:
```json
{
  "compilerOptions": {
    "baseUrl": ".",
    "paths": {
      "@/*": ["src/*"]
    }
  }
}
```

Add a defensive check and provide a clear error message:
```tsx
const rootEl = document.getElementById('root');
if (!rootEl) {
  throw new Error('Root element not found. Ensure <div id="root"></div> exists in index.html');
}
createRoot(rootEl).render(
  <StrictMode>
    <App />
  </StrictMode>
);
```
